1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,824
This tutorial covers three changes to a
tenancy contract,

2
00:00:03,824 --> 00:00:07,223
and what each one writes in the books.

3
00:00:07,223 --> 00:00:08,498
First, a renewal.

4
00:00:08,498 --> 00:00:12,322
As the Company Admin, open Omar Haddad's
contract for

5
00:00:12,322 --> 00:00:16,146
R-101, which ends on 30 September, and
choose Renew.

6
00:00:16,146 --> 00:00:21,244
The new term runs from 1 October 2026 to
30 September 2027.

7
00:00:21,244 --> 00:00:24,219
Choose By percent and enter 5: the

8
00:00:24,219 --> 00:00:26,768
rent moves from 72,000 to 75,600.

9
00:00:26,768 --> 00:00:29,742
Keep Carry deposit forward, add a Renewal

10
00:00:29,742 --> 00:00:32,292
Fee of 525, and select Renew.

11
00:00:32,292 --> 00:00:35,691
The renewal is a new draft contract, with

12
00:00:35,691 --> 00:00:39,090
its own cheques and its own posting
journal.

13
00:00:39,090 --> 00:00:42,064
Priya Raman's contract shows the finished
result.

14
00:00:42,064 --> 00:00:46,313
Its header reads Rent revised from 64,000
to 67,200, plus

15
00:00:46,313 --> 00:00:50,562
5 percent, and links back to the contract
it renewed.

16
00:00:50,562 --> 00:00:53,961
The Renewal Fee is income when charged,
and

17
00:00:53,961 --> 00:00:57,360
it is not copied at the next renewal.

18
00:00:57,360 --> 00:01:01,609
In its journals, the deposit carried
forward is a journal

19
00:01:01,609 --> 00:01:05,433
voucher: the deposit never left, so 3,200
moves from

20
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:09,257
the old contract's Security Deposit to the
new one's.

21
00:01:09,257 --> 00:01:10,956
Second, a rent-free period.

22
00:01:10,956 --> 00:01:14,356
Sahara Design Studio took office BC-302 at
96,000

23
00:01:14,356 --> 00:01:17,755
a year, with February free for their
fit-out.

24
00:01:17,755 --> 00:01:22,004
The concession is 7,364.38, so the rent
line posts 88,635.62,

25
00:01:22,004 --> 00:01:26,252
and VAT of 4,431.78 is charged on that
lower figure.

26
00:01:26,252 --> 00:01:31,351
Income is spread evenly over the whole
term, the free month included.

27
00:01:31,351 --> 00:01:33,051
Third, a unit transfer.

28
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:37,300
Open Mohammed Al Rashid's contract for
R-202 and choose Transfer.

29
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:41,548
He moves to R-203 after the night of 30
September.

30
00:01:41,548 --> 00:01:44,948
The preview lists his cheques, each to
carry

31
00:01:44,948 --> 00:01:47,922
to the new contract, keep or return.

32
00:01:47,922 --> 00:01:52,171
It shows what he has earned on the current
unit,

33
00:01:52,171 --> 00:01:55,995
the 13,264.93 he has paid ahead, which
moves to

34
00:01:55,995 --> 00:01:59,819
the new contract, and his 3,900 deposit,
carried across.

35
00:01:59,819 --> 00:02:03,218
There is no gap to collect, and nothing

36
00:02:03,218 --> 00:02:06,192
is posted until the new contract is.
